{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Nine hundred [Dm]i[C6]ron chariots [Dm]rolled
[C6]Cruel op[Dm]pres[C6]sion lasted twenty [Dm]years [C6]
[Dm]Israel [C6]cried out to the [Dm][C6]Lord
Jabin [Bb]reigned [C]in Hazor with [Dm]fear
[C6]Si[Bb]sera commanded the [C]army
Ha-[Bb]ros-heth-ha-go-yim [A]was his home
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]He [C6]asked for water [Dm]she [C6]gave him [Dm]milk
[C6]In a bowl fit for [Dm]a [C6]prince
Her hand reached [Dm]for [C6]the tent peg
[Bb]Her right hand for the hammer
She struck Sisera [C]crushed his head
Shattered and [Dm]pierced [C6]his [C6]tem[Dm]ple
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C6]Barak went up [Dm]Mount [Dm]Tabor
Si[C6]sera sum[Dm]moned [C6]his [Dm]troops
From [C6]Kishon River to [Dm]the battle
[C6][Bb]The Lord routed his [Dm]for[C6]ces
[Bb]Sisera fled on [C]foot
Left his [Bb]chariot be[A]hind in dust
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]He asked [C6]for water she [Dm]gave [C6]him milk
[Dm]In [C6]a bowl fit for a [Dm]prince [C6]
[Dm]Her [C6]hand reached for [Dm]the [C6]tent peg
Her right [Bb]hand for the hammer
She struck Sisera crushed his [C]head
Shattered and pierced his [Dm]temple
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Jael covered him with a blan[C]ket
He lay [Dm]fast [C]asleep and exhaust[Bb]ed
She drove the peg into the [C]ground
So he [Dm]died [C]in the [Bb]tent
Barak came and found him [C]there
Dead with the peg through his [Dm]head
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Most blessed [C6]of women [Dm]be Jael
[C6]Most [Dm]blessed of [C6]women in [Dm]tents
[C6]Sis[Dm]era's [C6]mother looked out the [Dm]win[C6]dow
[Bb]Wailing for the spoil and the cloth
{end_of_verse}

